From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:48:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 57/57] hottyterm: emoji draw from OpenMoji on every platform

The emoji fallback is OpenMoji 17.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0), the release's
openmoji-font.zip as a lazy dependency: OpenMoji Color in the format the
platform's rasterizer draws (sbix for CoreText, CBDT for FreeType) and
OpenMoji Black for text presentation. They replace Noto Color Emoji and
Noto Emoji, which stay for the tests, and macOS no longer adds Apple
Color Emoji ahead of them, so an emoji looks alike everywhere, and as
hotty-blitz's surfaces draw it. A font-family or font-codepoint-map
that names another emoji font still wins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
